From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: arm64: Add a camera module prober for the Huawei
 Matebook E Go

The Huawei Matebook E Go is built with one of two front camera modules,
a Hynix HI846 or a Samsung S5K4H7, and one of two rear camera modules,
an OmniVision OV13B10 or a Samsung S5K3L6. The two modules for one
connector share its supplies, reset line and MCLK, and answer at
different addresses on its CCI bus.

With all four enabled in the device tree, every sensor driver powers its
connector, and the drivers of the modules that are not fitted fail to
probe. The reset line of a connector then has two consumers, and the
two rear modules need different MCLK rates.

Have the device tree describe the modules with the status
"fail-needs-probe" instead, and probe them as the ChromeOS hardware
prober does: power each connector with the supplies, reset line and MCLK
of one of its module nodes, find the address that answers and enable
that node, so that only the fitted module's sensor driver probes. The
connectors are on CCI buses, hence i2c_of_probe_component_on_bus().

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/Kconfig                |  16 +
 drivers/platform/arm64/Makefile               |   1 +
 .../arm64/huawei-gaokun3-camera-prober.c      | 363 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 380 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun3-camera-prober.c

